```python
import re

code = """
        // @@@ If the return value is false, last position of x in old list is >= -1
"""

matches = re.findall(r'@@@\s*(.*?)(?=\n|$)', code, re.DOTALL)

for match in matches:
    print(f'Debug.Assert({match});')
```

This code finds all occurrences of "@@@" followed by any number of any characters (`.*?`), as long as they are not a newline or the end of the string (`(?=\n|$)`). The `re.DOTALL` flag is used to make the dot in the regex match any character, including a newline.

